# Monadle Chat Backend Structure

The backend of Monadle Chat is built with Deno, providing server-side functionality for the chat application.

## Directory Structure Overview

```
server/
├── .vscode/              - VS Code editor settings
├── node_modules/         - Project dependencies
├── scripts/             - Utility scripts for server operations
├── src/                 - Source code
│   ├── agents/          - Code related to agentic workflows
│   ├── db/              - Database configuration and schemas
│   │                      (drizzle schema, migrations, clients)
│   ├── functions/       - Reusable server functions
│   ├── middleware/      - Request middleware
│   ├── routes/          - API endpoint definitions
│   └── types/           - Server specific types
├── .env                 - Environment variables
├── .env.example         - Example environment variables template
├── deno.json           - Deno configuration
├── deno.lock           - Dependency lock file
├── drizzle.config.ts   - Database ORM configuration
├── main.ts             - Main server entry point
└── README.md           - Backend documentation
```
